{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Intervals","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HardWallProjection","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.RoundedWaterfillExchange"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.rev_two_sided_excess_bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.rev_two_sided_excess_bracket","kind":"theorem","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RevBoundedExcessAssembly.lean#L314-L340","doc":"**Two-sided `O(1)` excess bracket (`−K₃ ≤ M_n − A√(2n) ≤ K₂`).**\nCombining `rev_upper_bound_assembly` (applied to an arbitrary maximiser reaching `Mn`) and\n`rev_lower_bound_assembly` (applied to the candidate shape `λ_{k,r}` with `shapeHookSum − Fn ≤ Mn`)\nplaces the excess `Mn − A√(2n)` inside the `n`-independent interval `[−K₃, K₂]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.rev_lower_bound_assembly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.rev_lower_bound_assembly","kind":"theorem","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RevBoundedExcessAssembly.lean#L291-L312","doc":"**Lower-bound assembly (`Ψ(λ_{k,r}) ≥ A√(2n) − K₃`, with `K₃ = 3A/2 + 2B + C`).**\nGiven the row-deleted staircase hook-sum inequality `staircaseSum (k − r) + staircaseSum r ≤\nshapeHookSum` (`StaircaseRowDeletedHook.rowDeleted_hookSum_ge`), the staircase lower bound\n`A m − B ≤ staircaseSum m` (`rem_m ≥ 0`), the one-body upper bound `Fn ≤ C`, and\n`√(2n) ≤ k + 3/2`, the shape's objective `shapeHookSum − Fn` is at least `A√(2n) − (3A/2 + 2B + C)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.rev_upper_bound_assembly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.rev_upper_bound_assembly","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RevBoundedExcessAssembly.lean#L266-L289","doc":"**Upper-bound assembly (`Ψ(λ) ≤ A√(2n) + K₂`).**\nCombining `coord_tradeoff_sum_le` (`≤ K₁`) and `extra_rows_tradeoff` (`≤ J`) with\n`l ≤ k + j`, `k ≤ √(2n)`, and `ε(1) ≤ F(n)` bounds any shape's objective `Ψ` by\n`A√(2n) + (S₂ + K₁ + J − ε(1))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.coord_tradeoff_sum_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.coord_tradeoff_sum_le","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RevBoundedExcessAssembly.lean#L236-L264","doc":"**Summed integer-grid coordinate trade-off (`K₁ = c₁ + c₀ c₁ / (2L)`).**\nSumming `RoundedWaterfillExchange.int_tradeoff` over `i ∈ s` with `0 ≤ ω i ≤ c0` and\n`∑ i ∈ s, ω i ≤ c1` bounds the total coordinate slack by `c1 + c0 * c1 / (2 * L)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.roundedWaterfill_pythagoras","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.roundedWaterfill_pythagoras","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RevBoundedExcessAssembly.lean#L217-L232","doc":"**Discrete Pythagoras for the explicit rounded water-fill `q_i = max(w_i, c_i)`.**\nDischarges both order hypotheses of `RoundedWaterfillExchange.rounded_pythagoras` from `w ≤ t`\nand `a ≤ c ≤ a + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.roundedWaterfill_le_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.roundedWaterfill_le_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RevBoundedExcessAssembly.lean#L203-L215","doc":"Second hypothesis of `rounded_pythagoras`: if `t` sits above the wall `w` (`w_i ≤ t_i`) and\n`c_i ≤ a + 1`, then any coordinate where `t_i < max(w_i, c_i)` must lie in the flat part and\nsatisfy `max(w_i, c_i) ≤ a + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.roundedWaterfill_ge_floor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.roundedWaterfill_ge_floor","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RevBoundedExcessAssembly.lean#L196-L200","doc":"First hypothesis of `rounded_pythagoras`: `a ≤ c_i` implies `a ≤ max(w_i, c_i)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.shiftDiff_le_of_roundedWaterfill","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.shiftDiff_le_of_roundedWaterfill","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RevBoundedExcessAssembly.lean#L187-L193","doc":"Consequently `Δ_k(t) ≤ Δ_k(t − q)` against the rounded water-fill `q = max(w, c)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.shiftDiff_roundedWaterfill_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.shiftDiff_roundedWaterfill_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RevBoundedExcessAssembly.lean#L181-L185","doc":"Monotonicity of `roundedWaterfill w c` ensures `Δ_k(q) ≤ 0` for every neighbour order `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.roundedWaterfill_monotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.roundedWaterfill_monotone","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RevBoundedExcessAssembly.lean#L175-L179","doc":"If both the wall `w` and the rounded flat profile `c` are monotone, then\n`roundedWaterfill w c` is monotone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.roundedWaterfill","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.roundedWaterfill","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RevBoundedExcessAssembly.lean#L170-L172","doc":"The explicit rounded water-fill profile `q_i = max(w_i, c_i)` built from a wall `w` and a\nrounded flat profile `c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.abs_sum_shiftDiff_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.abs_sum_shiftDiff_le","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RevBoundedExcessAssembly.lean#L156-L166","doc":"**Absolute-value bound on `Δ_k(d)` via head and tail.**  Because the middle cancels,\n`|Δ_k(d)|` is at most the `ℓ¹` sum of `d` over the first `min(k, L − k)` and last `min(k, L − k)`\ncoordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.sum_shiftDiff_eq_head_sub_tail","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.sum_shiftDiff_eq_head_sub_tail","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RevBoundedExcessAssembly.lean#L139-L154","doc":"**Middle cancellation of `Δ_k(d)`.**  For `k ≤ L`, the neighbour-order-`k` difference sum\n`Σ_{i < L−k} (d_i − d_{i+k})` telescopes to the sum of the first `m_k = min(k, L − k)` coordinates\nminus the last `m_k` coordinates; the overlap `Ico k (L − k)` cancels when `2k ≤ L`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.sum_shiftDiff_eq_Ico","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.sum_shiftDiff_eq_Ico","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RevBoundedExcessAssembly.lean#L129-L137","doc":"Reindexing the shifted sum: `Σ_{i < m} (d_i − d_{i+k}) = Σ_{i < m} d_i − Σ_{k ≤ i < m+k} d_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.oneBody_sub_pair_le_of_tangent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.oneBody_sub_pair_le_of_tangent","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RevBoundedExcessAssembly.lean#L106-L125","doc":"**One-body minus pair sum upper bound.**  Combining `pair_sum_ge_of_tangent` and\n`even_tail_le_weighted_sum` with the one-body ceiling `oneBody i ≤ A + E₂` yields\n`Σ_i oneBody_i − Σ_{k,i} pairTerm_{k,i} ≤ L · A + S₂ + Σ_k slope_k · Δ_k(t)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.even_tail_le_weighted_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.even_tail_le_weighted_sum","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RevBoundedExcessAssembly.lean#L73-L104","doc":"**Why `L · E₂ − Σ_{k<L} (L − k) ε(2k) ≤ S₂`.**  For `1 ≤ k < L` the coefficient of `ε(2k)` is\n`L − (L − k) = k`, and in the tail `L ≤ k < N` we have `L · ε(2k) ≤ k · ε(2k)` since `ε(2k) ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.pair_sum_ge_of_tangent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RevBoundedExcessAssembly.pair_sum_ge_of_tangent","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RevBoundedExcessAssembly.lean#L57-L71","doc":"**Tangent-line lower bound on the pair sum.**  If every pair at neighbour order `k ∈ [1, L)`\nand row `i < L − k` satisfies `epsEven k - slope k * (t i - t (i + k)) ≤ pairTerm k i`, then\nsumming over pairs gives `(L − k) · epsEven k − slope k · Δ_k(t)` at each order `k`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}